;; Reviewed 2026-10-11 by the user (written by Claude, from the VAX
;; architecture and the guest runs). Why this is right:
;; - Case 11 reads with SYSTEM.GET at address 0, which VMS leaves
;;   unmapped (page 0 of P0 space is no access): an access violation
;;   (ACCVIO, virtual address 00000000), VMS's counterpart of LLVM's
;;   SIGSEGV (status 139; language-extensions.md, "What traps, and what
;;   does not").
;; - VMS's own message, then its traceback; tools/vax-suite masks the
;;   addresses.
;; - The same under -O2 and -OC.
%SYSTEM-F-ACCVIO, access violation, reason mask=00, virtual address=00000000, PC=xxxxxxxx, PSL=xxxxxxxx
%TRACE-F-TRACEBACK, symbolic stack dump follows
module name     routine name                     line       rel PC    abs PC

NOTRAP          POC_CODE                                   xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
NOTRAP          NOTRAP_MAIN                                xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
